    "id": "lem:multiplier-primitives",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(N=nm\\), \\(d=|\\mathcal G_n|\\), and order cells by \\(o\\).  Under sequential randomization, overlap, bounded outcomes, polynomial family growth, dense average-scale loadings, and variance nondegeneracy, \\((X_{k,g},\\mathbb G_k)_{k=1}^N\\) is a \\(d\\)-dimensional martingale-difference array,\n\\[\n N^{-1}\\sum_{k=1}^NE_P[\\lVert X_k\\rVert_\\infty^3]=O(1)\\le N^{1/8},\n \\qquad \\log^{7/2}d=o(N^{1/4}),\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n \\max_{g,g'\\in\\mathcal G_n}\\left|N^{-1}\\sum_{k=1}^N\n \\{X_{k,g}X_{k,g'}-E_P[X_{k,g}X_{k,g'}\\mid\\mathbb G_{k-1}]\\}\\right|\n =O_P\\!\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\log(ed)}N}\\right)\n =o_P(N^{-1/8}\\log^{-2}(eNd)).\n\\]\nThese oracle conclusions do not assert consistency or positivity of the leave-one-cell-out residual studentizers.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "n",
      "m",
      "G",
      "ord",
      "Xnorm",
      "Gglobal",
      "P",
      "g",
      "gprime",
      "soracle",
      "i",
      "j",
      "B",
      "q"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:global-filtration",
      "def:predictable-class",
      "def:ipw-score",
      "lem:ipw-identification",
      "ass:polynomial-family",
      "ass:average-loadings",
